     "result_text_tail": " words.\n- **Executive summary trimmed so it reads at 12 pt or larger.** Two points from the source summary are now only on their own slides: \"synergy evidence is correlation only\" (slide 10) and \"a build ships late 2028\" (slide 13).\n- **Two exhibits changed form:**\n  - Slide 7's three-bar chart is folded into the bridge table as a \"Sellers' pitch\" row.\n  - Slide 15's ceiling calculation is now a strip of number cards under the term sheet.\n- **Calculations page split in two** (pages 21\u201322) so the table stays readable.\n- **Workaround: post-render step.** Tables can't show two-decimal figures like 0.07 or 0.92 as linked numbers, so those are typed into the cells. That left 14 slides with no source line and empty workbook sheets. A script I wrote (`work/postprocess.py`) fixes both after rendering, using a hand-made list of which numbers appear on each slide. Running `render.py` on its own will undo that fix.\n\n**Warnings left in QA:** most slides are dense (over 1,300 characters) because I kept every point from the source. Some title numbers appear in table text rather than as linked values. Two pack excerpts write the number as a word (\"eighteen months\", \"two years\").\n\nI couldn't preview the slides as images: there's no LibreOffice here and the sandbox blocks opening apps. I checked the layout through the renderer's measurements and its warnings. Open the `.pptx` once in PowerPoint before you send it.\n\nI can switch the theme or tighten the densest slides (10, 11, 14) if you want."
